From 388fa9a0796f6d5cea1e54e8352ff87fd67c5c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elliot Shepherd <elliot@jarofworms.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:44:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] snapshot: stream only the RAM pages that differ from a
 caller's base

FINISH_SAVE_DELTA <dir> <table length>, followed by a page table, finishes
a prepared save as a delta. The table describes the caller's base image:
for each 4 KiB page of the image, whether it reads as zeros, holds data
with a seeded XXH3-128, or is unknown. The VMM reads guest RAM in 2 MiB
blocks on four threads, with the same readers a full save uses, hashes each
page, and for each block with a changed page streams a frame: the block
number, a bitmap of its changed pages, a bitmap of those that hold data,
and the bytes of the data pages only. It then publishes checkpoint.bin and
manifest.bin without a memory image. The caller writes the pages into its
base; the VMM never gets a descriptor of it. A table for an image of
another length is ignored, so every page is sent.

SAVE_DELTA_CAPABILITIES answers "OK delta-v2". Linux only.
